; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR STARSHIP  -  the COSMAC ELF logo, any key to quit   (VT100)
; ==========================================================================
; The COSMAC ELF starship, drawn once and left on the screen. Any key clears it and
; returns to the monitor.
;
; THE PATTERN IS CRAIG'S. It lives in APPLICATIONS/Starship 2.txt, which he drew by
; editing the earlier traced version, and this program is generated from that file - so
; the file is the thing to edit, not this listing. Each line there is |<interior>| and
; interior column N is screen column N, which puts the drawing in columns 3-80 of lines
; 1-23. (The tracer that produced the earlier artwork is in git history, at
; starship_art.py in 6bb4217, if the geometry ever needs re-deriving from the photo.)
;
; TWO KINDS OF CONTENT. A '#' is a lit cell, painted as a SPACE IN REVERSE VIDEO
; (ESC[7m), which gives a solid block on anything back to a real VT100. Anything else is
; literal text: Craig's 'STELLAR EDITION' caption on line 22. Reverse video is turned OFF
; before the caption is printed, or it would come out as a solid bar.
;
; THE PICTURE IS A RUN TABLE, not a bitmap. A bitmap of 80x23 would be 230 bytes that
; still needs unpacking bit by bit; instead every unbroken horizontal stretch of lit
; cells is three bytes - line, first column, length - and a line byte of $00 ends the
; table. 108 stretches, 325 bytes, 426 lit cells, and the renderer is a dozen commands:
; read three bytes with READIDX, position the cursor, emit that many spaces, repeat.
;
; A run costs the same three bytes however long it is, so the long hull and nacelle
; lines are nearly free. Painting the whole picture is about 1305 bytes of output.
;
; ADDRESSES. The READIDX base in the code is PROGRAM-RELATIVE - $0900 means $4900 at
; run time - but the data D-lines below carry the ABSOLUTE address. Writing the table at
; the relative address would drop it on the firmware. The caption sits at $4A80, clear
; of the run table, which now reaches $4A44; the builder asserts they cannot overlap.
;
; Any key quits: SERIN waits cooperatively, yielding to the scheduler rather than
; spinning, so other VMs keep running while the picture is up.
;
; Sim-verified: the escape stream replayed into a 23x80 screen reproduces Craig's
; pattern CELL FOR CELL, all 1840 of them, caption included; and the keypress restores
; normal video, shows the cursor, clears the screen and homes.
;
; The picture as it appears:
;
; |                                                                                  |
; |    ##### ##### ##### #   # ##### #####                                           |
; |    #   # #   # #     ## ## #   # #   #                                           |
; |    #     #   # ##### # # # ##### #                                               |
; |    #   # #   #     # #   # #   # #   #                                           |
; |    ##### ##### ##### #   # #   # #####                                           |
; |                                                                   ########       |
; |                                         ######################################## |
; |                  ###                   ##                                     ## |
; |             #############              ##                                    ##  |
; |   ############         ############     ########  #############################  |
; |   #             #####             ##           #  ##                             |
; |   ############         ############            #  ##                             |
; |              ##########  ##     ##             #  ##                             |
; |                 #####     ##     ##            #  ##         ##### #     #####   |
; |                            ##     ##           #  ##         #     #     #       |
; |                          #######################  #####      ####  #     ####    |
; |                        ####                          ###     #     #     #       |
; |                       ####  ###########               ##     ##### ##### #       |
; |                        ###                 #############                         |
; |                         ####       #########                                     |
; |                            #########                         STELLAR EDITION     |
; |                                                                                  |
;
; 81 STELLAR commands, $4000-$40B2 (179 bytes of code).
; Data at $4900, 325 bytes, past the end marker.
; Data at $4A80, 16 bytes, past the end marker.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; D 4000 CD             START                  Start of program, and run the label pre-pass
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A        Ten, for splitting numbers into digits
; D 4005 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 4007 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 4009 CA 32          SEROUTI 32             2
; D 400B CA 4A          SEROUTI 4A             J - clear the screen
; D 400D CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 400F CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 4011 CA 3F          SEROUTI 3F             ?
; D 4013 CA 32          SEROUTI 32             2
; D 4015 CA 35          SEROUTI 35             5
; D 4017 CA 6C          SEROUTI 6C             l - hide the cursor
; D 4019 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 401B CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 401D CA 37          SEROUTI 37             7
; D 401F CA 6D          SEROUTI 6D             m - reverse video: a space is now a lit block
; D 4021 11 09 00 00    LOADXI R9 0000         Index into the run table
; D 4025 2E 09 09 00    READIDX R9 0900        The line this run sits on
; D 4029 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000            Zero ends the table
; D 402C A0 00 52       IFTRUEI SHOWN
; D 402F 21 0D          COPYAX 0D              into R13 for POSXY
; D 4031 42 09          INCX R9
; D 4033 2E 09 09 00    READIDX R9 0900        The column it starts at
; D 4037 21 0E          COPYAX 0E              into R14
; D 4039 42 09          INCX R9
; D 403B 2E 09 09 00    READIDX R9 0900        and how many cells long it is
; D 403F 21 0A          COPYAX 0A              into R10
; D 4041 42 09          INCX R9
; D 4043 BD 00 91       CALL POSXY
; D 4046 CA 20          SEROUTI 20             A space in reverse video is a lit block
; D 4048 43 0A          DECX R10
; D 404A 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10
; D 404C A1 00 46       IFFALSEI CELL
; D 404F B0 00 25       GAL NEXT
; D 4052 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 4054 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 4056 CA 30          SEROUTI 30             0
; D 4058 CA 6D          SEROUTI 6D             m - normal video for the caption
; D 405A 11 0D 00 16    LOADXI R13 0016        Caption line
; D 405E 11 0E 00 3E    LOADXI R14 003E        and column
; D 4062 BD 00 91       CALL POSXY
; D 4065 11 0B 0A 80    LOADXI R11 0A80        -> 'STELLAR EDITION'
; D 4069 C1 0B          PRINTSTR R11
; D 406B CB             SERIN                  Wait for any key - SERIN yields, so other VMs keep running
; D 406C CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 406E CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 4070 CA 30          SEROUTI 30             0
; D 4072 CA 6D          SEROUTI 6D             m - back to normal video
; D 4074 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 4076 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 4078 CA 3F          SEROUTI 3F             ?
; D 407A CA 32          SEROUTI 32             2
; D 407C CA 35          SEROUTI 35             5
; D 407E CA 68          SEROUTI 68             h - show the cursor again
; D 4080 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 4082 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 4084 CA 32          SEROUTI 32             2
; D 4086 CA 4A          SEROUTI 4A             J - clear the screen
; D 4088 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 408A CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 408C CA 48          SEROUTI 48             H - cursor home
; D 408E F0 00 00       BREAK                  End of program
; D 4091 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 4093 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 4095 4D DF          DIVXY R13 R15
; D 4097 25             COPYMAA
; D 4098 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 409B C9             SEROUT                 Tens
; D 409C 27             COPYREMA
; D 409D 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 40A0 C9             SEROUT                 Units
; D 40A1 CA 3B          SEROUTI 3B             ;
; D 40A3 4D EF          DIVXY R14 R15
; D 40A5 25             COPYMAA
; D 40A6 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 40A9 C9             SEROUT                 Tens
; D 40AA 27             COPYREMA
; D 40AB 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 40AE C9             SEROUT                 Units
; D 40AF CA 48          SEROUTI 48             H
; D 40B1 BE 00          RETURN
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; CODE  -  download this block
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

